#  Supplement to usfm.sty, appended to it by build.rs before the sheet is
#  parsed. usfm.sty is Paratext's file, kept byte-for-byte as distributed
#  (see NOTICE.md), so everything we add or correct lives here instead.
#
#  Every entry cites the authority it comes from: tcdocs' grammar/usx.rnc,
#  which is the schema this parser is tested against. A `\Marker` that already
#  exists in usfm.sty amends that entry rather than replacing it, so only the
#  fields written here change.
#
#  Character-style entries reuse the `\OccursUnder` list of `\tl`, which is the
#  list usfm.sty gives every member of `Char.char.style.enum`.

#  `ipc`, "Introduction prose paragraph, centred", in Para.para.style.enum
#  (usx.rnc). Modelled on `\ipr`, its right-aligned sibling.
\Marker ipc
\Name ipc - Introduction - Paragraph - centred
\Description Introduction prose paragraph, centred
\OccursUnder id
\Rank 6
\TextType Other
\TextProperties paragraph publishable vernacular
\StyleType Paragraph
\FontSize 12

#  `wl`, "Indicating words in a foreign language and perhaps script", in
#  Char.char.style.enum (usx.rnc), with `lang` as its default attribute.
\Marker wl
\Endmarker wl*
\Name wl...wl* - Special Text - Word List Entry
\Description Indicating words in a foreign language and perhaps script
\OccursUnder ip im ipi imi ipq imq ipr iq iq1 iq2 iq3 io io1 io2 io3 io4 ms ms1 ms2 s s1 s2 s3 s4 cd sp d lh li li1 li2 li3 li4 lf lim lim1 lim2 lim3 lim4 m mi nb p pc ph phi pi pi1 pi2 pi3 pr pmo pm pmc pmr po q q1 q2 q3 q4 qc qr qd qm qm1 qm2 qm3 cls tr th1 th2 th3 th4 thr1 thr2 thr3 thr4 tc1 tc2 tc3 tc4 tcr1 tcr2 tcr3 tcr4 f fe ef efe NEST
\TextType VerseText
\TextProperties publishable vernacular
\StyleType Character
\FontSize 12

#  `ta`, "Text alternatives", in Char.char.style.enum (usx.rnc) beside `\w`
#  and `\rb`. Its attributes are the `a-*` namespace and it has no default.
\Marker ta
\Endmarker ta*
\Name ta...ta* - Special Text - Text Alternatives
\Description Text alternatives, named by an a- attribute per alternative
\OccursUnder ip im ipi imi ipq imq ipr iq iq1 iq2 iq3 io io1 io2 io3 io4 ms ms1 ms2 s s1 s2 s3 s4 cd sp d lh li li1 li2 li3 li4 lf lim lim1 lim2 lim3 lim4 m mi nb p pc ph phi pi pi1 pi2 pi3 pr pmo pm pmc pmr po q q1 q2 q3 q4 qc qr qd qm qm1 qm2 qm3 cls tr th1 th2 th3 th4 thr1 thr2 thr3 thr4 tc1 tc2 tc3 tc4 tcr1 tcr2 tcr3 tcr4 f fe ef efe NEST
\TextType VerseText
\TextProperties publishable vernacular
\StyleType Character
\FontSize 12

#  `xta` under `\ex` as well as `\x`. usx.rnc puts every CrossReferenceChar
#  style under CrossReference.style.enum, which is `x` and `ex`; usfm.sty
#  already lists both on `\xo` and `\xt` and only forgets them on `\xta`.
\Marker xta
\OccursUnder x ex

#  `s5`, a level-5 section heading. Not in usfm.sty or usx.rnc: unfoldingWord's
#  texts (tcdocs' `usfmjsTests`, the `doo43` samples) write `\s5` as a chunk
#  break, and this entry, carried in usfm.sty itself before it was restored to
#  the distributed file, keeps it a paragraph rather than an unknown marker.
\Marker s5
\Name s5 - Heading - Section Level 5
\Description A section heading, level 5
\OccursUnder c
\TextType Section
\TextProperties paragraph publishable vernacular level_5
\StyleType Paragraph
\FontSize 12
\Italic
\Justification Left
\SpaceBefore 6
\SpaceAfter 3
